r": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AHDmF8JF7TtA4HZvdghu4m", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 11040, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013qDmdfZzuuBETuhouAQUEy", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 11340, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013qDmdfZzuuBETuhouAQUEy", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 11340, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013qDmdfZzuuBETuhouAQUEy", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 14539, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QBAEy2aXSehLffzSA8Qemh", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18539, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QBAEy2aXSehLffzSA8Qemh", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18539, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QBAEy2aXSehLffzSA8Qemh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20520, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01VTjMUcQUqQeAf9hMnAAdDc", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20820, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VTjMUcQUqQeAf9hMnAAdDc", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20820, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VTjMUcQUqQeAf9hMnAAdDc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20820, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GS3o7HjtXmSpSc4b3k7dnu", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21120, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GS3o7HjtXmSpSc4b3k7dnu", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21120, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GS3o7HjtXmSpSc4b3k7dnu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 26226, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01J3QWBYsw9MbiEtdGyVry9v", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second attempt finished successfully. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why it was promoted when the RC was unhealthy in staging. Also look into the orchestrator error during the rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56826, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J3QWBYsw9MbiEtdGyVry9v", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56826, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J3QWBYsw9MbiEtdGyVry9v", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58955, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01J4YSdcHEUKoy2TtYVdb8pF", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59255, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J4YSdcHEUKoy2TtYVdb8pF", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59255, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J4YSdcHEUKoy2TtYVdb8pF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63849, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. It was healthy before, so this rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1, so I tried once more and it worked.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list: it had been created, so I didn't open a second one and send a duplicate page.\n- The summary covers the rollback, the error during it and the current state. It also lists next steps: find out why v2.3.1 failed, why it was released when its candidate was unhealthy in staging, and what caused the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SsGaoKGZiL3aDK9ZsqzFFf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y5Q1WYX84MrnGyDLb3WoAg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AHDmF8JF7TtA4HZvdghu4m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013qDmdfZzuuBETuhouAQUEy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. v2.3.0 was healthy in production, so I'll retry the rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QBAEy2aXSehLffzSA8Qemh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VTjMUcQUqQeAf9hMnAAdDc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GS3o7HjtXmSpSc4b3k7dnu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J3QWBYsw9MbiEtdGyVry9v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second attempt finished successfully. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why it was promoted when the RC was unhealthy in staging. Also look into the orchestrator error during the rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01J4YSdcHEUKoy2TtYVdb8pF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. It was healthy before, so this rollback didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1, so I tried once more and it worked.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list: it had been created, so I didn't open a second one and send a duplicate page.\n- The summary covers the rollback, the error during it and the current state. It also lists next steps: find out why v2.3.1 failed, why it was released when its candidate was unhealthy in staging, and what caused the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}